- op: discuss  # c311
  at: '2026-09-22T07:30:36Z'  # c311
  by: agent  # c311
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c311
  clock: 15  # c311
  nonce: c311  # c311
  message: "REOPENED to violated on POSITIVE EVIDENCE, not on non-reproduction. Owner\nauthorised the reopen after I surfaced the closure-evidence problem.\n\nTHE STATEMENT: \"Every Edge produced by a linker should record which Symbols\n(and possibly which Edges) the linker consumed as derivation inputs.\"\n\nWHY THE 2026-07-26 CLOSURE DOES NOT ESTABLISH IT. It cites\ntest_edge_derived_from.py::test_all_linker_edge_creates_pass_derived_from and\nreports \"91/91 Edge.create sites ... stamp it with real consumed-id lists\".\nThat test's entire predicate is `if \"derived_from\" not in kwarg_names`. It\nasserts the KEYWORD IS PRESENT. It cannot distinguish derived_from=[src, dst]\nfrom a list naming a genuinely consumed third input, so it cannot witness the\nsemantic half of the statement -- which is the half the statement is about.\nUnder the Closure-Evidence Discipline a syntactic proxy may supplement but\nnever substitute. The closure note also states \"WI-latup not in repo\";\nWI-latup-nufab exists and is open.\n\nTHE COUNTEREXAMPLE, chosen because it survives the fair objection.\nI did NOT reopen on the bare fact that 86 of 93 sites pass [src, dst]. For\ncontainment-linker that may be the HONEST and COMPLETE answer -- a contains\nedge really is derived from just the parent and the child, and there is no\nthird input to name. Same for decorator-dispatch-linker: its join key\n`dec_name` is read off metadata carried by the two endpoint symbols, so a\nreader holding the endpoints can recover it.\n\ntype-hierarchy-linker is the case that cannot be defended that way. Its own\nmodule docstring, step 1: \"Build inheritance maps from `extends` and\n`implements` EDGES\". It joins a parent method to an overriding method BECAUSE\nan extends/implements edge relates their classes, then emits\n\n    derived_from=[parent_method.id, override.id]      (type_hierarchy.py:628)\n\nnaming neither that edge nor the two class symbols. The deciding record is a\nTHIRD object that is NOT reachable from the endpoints: given only\n(parent_method, override), a reader cannot recover WHICH inheritance path\njustified the dispatch, and for a class with several bases or a deep hierarchy\nthat path is genuinely lost.\n\nMEASURED on a current self-survey:\n    type-hierarchy-linker edges                     342\n      ...whose derived_from is endpoints-only       342   (all of them)\n    extends/implements edges present in the graph   259   (250 extends, 9 implements)\n                                                          -- the consumed records, unnamed\n\n  Worked example from that survey:\n    src  IToken.transfer:method      (solidity/Contract.sol:8)\n    dst  Token.transfer:method       (solidity/Contract.sol:27-30)\n    derived_from  [IToken.transfer, Token.transfer]\n  The `implements` edge Token -> IToken is what made this edge exist. It is in\n  the graph. It is not in derived_from.\n\nThis is also exactly the clause the item's OWN 2026-06-05 validation recorded as\nunexercised -- \"the '(or Edge)' clause is unexercised\", blind severity 4, which\nmoved this row pending_validation -> violated before the 2026-07-26 closure\nreversed it on the syntactic test.\n\nWHAT IS GENUINELY SATISFIED, stated so the reopen is not read as wholesale:\ninherited-calls-linker (329 edges) and method-call-recovery-linker (62) DO name\nreal consumed inputs beyond their endpoints -- 391 edges, 0.2% of 190,109. The\nstatement is a UNIVERSAL (\"Every Edge\"), and 342 counterexamples falsify it.\n\nNOT A REGRESSION SINCE THE CLOSURE: between the 2026-06-05 validation and now\nthe count of genuinely-provenanced edges moved 0 -> 391, i.e. 2 of 58 linker\nfiles. Real progress, and far short of the statement.\n\nTHE COUPLING THAT HAS TO BE RESOLVED FIRST, which is why WI-latup is not a\nsweep: where [src, dst] IS the honest answer, the right outcome is to record\nNOTHING rather than invent a third input -- but the guard test above requires\nevery linker Edge.create to pass derived_from=, so \"record nothing\" fails it.\nThe test that closed this item is what keeps the field vacuous. Any repair has\nto decide that first.\n\nLive work: WI-latup (population half; disclosure half shipped 2026-09-22 --\nexplain --provenance no longer presents an endpoints-only value as a chain)."  # c311
- op: discuss  # dd2d
  at: '2026-09-22T21:36:31Z'  # dd2d
  by: agent  # dd2d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dd2d
  clock: 16  # dd2d
  nonce: dd2d  # dd2d
  message: "PARTIAL, MERGED as PR #1134 (562e5a3b8b). Status stays `violated`: 9 linker sites are DECLARED `incomplete`, so the statement (\"Every Edge produced by a linker should record which Symbols/Edges the linker consumed\") is still false for them. They are named below.\n\nTHE GUARD NOW READS THE VALUE. test_edge_derived_from.py::test_every_linker_edge_creates_states_its_consumed_inputs replaces the presence-only test. A site whose `derived_from` restates only its own src/dst expressions, or is empty, must carry an in-call declaration: `# derived-from endpoints|consumed-none|incomplete: <reason>`. A declaration on a value that already names more is refused as stale. It is STILL a syntactic check of a semantic claim. It cannot verify that a declaration is true, only that one was made where the value alone says nothing, and the test docstring says so.\n\nRULE DECIDED (ir.py, spec §9). `derived_from` names the INPUT records whose presence decided the edge. Ids the linker MINTED in the same run are not consumed and are omitted. inheritance.py:350's external placeholder was the precedent. `[]` means \"consumed no graph record\" and is distinct from `null`. Schema 0.20.12 -> 0.20.13 drops `minItems: 1`. This answers the coupling WI-latup raised (\"record nothing would fail the guard\"). Honest endpoints-only stays as a DECLARED positive value rather than becoming None. None would have merged \"a linker said the endpoints are the whole derivation\" with \"no statement\", which is the absent-vs-empty shape again.\n\nTHE COUNTEREXAMPLE IS CURED, WITH BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE. Fresh self-survey, compared against a baseline of dev b95e0d19ef in a worktree:\n  type-hierarchy-linker   342/342 endpoints-only  ->  342/342 chains naming the admitted extends/implements edges\n  all real chains         399 -> 840, every one naming a consumed EDGE\n  per-linker edge counts  unchanged (containment +30 comes from the PR's own new test code)\nTests: TestDerivedFromNamesInheritancePath (one hop, three hops child-first, and the dispatch gate). The gate test was mutation-checked: iterating raw inheritance edges instead of admitted ones turns it red.\n\nSITES, from an AST diff against dev (not a hand tally) -- 86 were endpoints-only:\n  17 now name the consumed record (12 unresolved/import edges, type_hierarchy path, rust_trait implements edge + struct, caddy struct, erlang otp module symbols, yjs gating dependency)\n  24 declared honest endpoints-only\n  36 dropped minted ids (20 -> [], 16 keep the one consumed endpoint)\n   9 declared INCOMPLETE -- the live violations of this row:\n     _third_party_bases, airflow_framework_dispatch, django_orm_dispatch, jackson_dispatch, kafka_streams_dispatch, grpc (base-chain struct) -- all walk the shared _transitive_bases BFS, which discards the ancestor and edge ids it visits\n     _view_template_core (the qualifying controller class)\n     di_resolution heuristic binding (the implements/extends edge build_interface_impl_map reads)\n     subprocess_cli fire.Fire target class\nNOT ASSERTED: that the 24 endpoints declarations are all true. Each rests on one read of the code by a research pass plus mine. The guard cannot check them."  # dd2d
